From ade013f96f6e1ca63ad9fc1f03148bc41ba92523 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aamir <aamir@tallow-lang.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:21:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/27] cli: add tallow `schema check`, `plan dry-run`, and
 local `extract` verbs

Three verbs that call the same loaders the runtime uses, so a second source of
truth for "is this schema usable" / "is this plan well-formed" cannot drift in.

  tallow schema check <f>   -> ExtractionSchema::from_v1_json, names the failing field
  tallow plan dry-run <f>   -> egresses nothing (statically barred + measured delta 0)
  tallow extract ...        -> local html + a v1 contract -> tallow.extraction_row.v1

`extract` is local-only by construction: the row contract pins mode=local_mock and
all non_claims false, so a live-crawl variant would be a lying artifact rather than
a feature. It writes rows AND a quarantine file, both in the gate's vocabulary.

Verified: cargo check --lib --bins RC=0; 22 tests (schema_cmd 6, plan_cmd 7,
extract_cmd 9); end-to-end both paths -- accepted page -> validator RC=0, missing
required field -> quarantined row with hard_errors=0.
